+## 2. What kind of article this is — read before §3
+
+⭐⭐ **It is a rebuttal by re-contextualisation, not by counter-evidence — and it says so.** Twelve of its fifteen moves are the same move: *the Father you cite was talking about pagans.* Only three advance positive evidence for ante-Nicene Christian liturgical incense (CA-4 Eusebius, CA-6 the liturgies, CA-7 Canon 3), and **all three are outside the repo's verified set**. ⭐ **That is the shape of the whole engagement: the part of the article the repo can already answer is the part that repeats what the repo already concedes, and the part the repo cannot yet answer is small, specific, and worth checking.**
+
+⚠️ **Register note, recorded because it affects how JD should handle the piece and not because it is an argument.** The article carries a persistent ad-hominem thread — Brattston "can bamboozle readers," his "mishandling… is painfully evident," "his training is in the field of law, not church history or Christian theology," and the closing call for retraction. ⛔ **`260835-49`'s independent check found 4 of 4 spot-checked citations verbatim-confirmed, both legal-historical dating disputes hedged by name, and the *De Idololatria* 11 handling "better than adequate."** ⭐ **Answering the tone would be a mistake; the repo's own audit is a better answer than any rejoinder, and it is quieter.**
